  "context": "## xSeil: Scenario-Based Planning and Human-Governed Computation\nA practical logistics system can calculate thousands or millions of technical possibilities while still leaving the most important decision to people: which competing operational objectives deserve priority. xSeil combined a reusable library of feasible route structures, scenario-dependent mathematical scoring, human selection of acceptable trade-offs, and iterative allocation that recalculated the consequences of each commitment. The result was an operational decision architecture connecting planning, vehicle resources, passengers and real-world execution.\nTags: Use cases and applications 27.59%; Decisions and responsibility 17.24%; Research and technical documentation 6.90%; Economics, costs and liquidity 13.79%; Mobility and infrastructure 34.48%\nCard: https://dakleyer.github.io/perspective-beyond/sources/xseil-scenario-based-planning-and-human-governed-computation-n2082/\nSource document: https://jubap.net/xseil-scenario-based-planning-human-governed-computation/\n\n",
